    <body>
        <segment id="1" parent="12" relname="background">The auto-correct feature can be useful and troublesome at the same time.</segment>
        <segment id="2" parent="12" relname="span">What I find annoying is the spellcheck feature in Microsoft Outlook.</segment>
        <segment id="3" parent="13" relname="span">I used to have this feature enable for all of my outgoing email.</segment>
        <segment id="4" parent="14" relname="span">After a while I would get so tired of it coming up each every time I compose a new message.</segment>
        <segment id="5" parent="4" relname="nonvolitional-result">This got to be quite annoying so I disabled it.</segment>
        <segment id="6" parent="15" relname="span">I know what you mean</segment>
        <segment id="7" parent="11" relname="span">when sometimes you don't want this feature to fix the problem.</segment>
        <segment id="8" parent="7" relname="elaboration">This is one of those things that some find to be a pro and others find it to be a con in usability.</segment>
        <group id="9" type="span"/>
        <group id="10" type="span" parent="9" relname="span"/>
        <group id="11" type="span" parent="6" relname="elaboration"/>
        <group id="12" type="span" parent="10" relname="span"/>
        <group id="13" type="span" parent="2" relname="elaboration"/>
        <group id="14" type="span" parent="3" relname="elaboration"/>
        <group id="15" type="span" parent="10" relname="summary"/>
    </body>
